source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: A line whose `|` stands behind spaces opens a row of its own rather than continuing the open row above it: Jira renders one data cell holding `a` and a forced newline, then a second row holding `b`. GFM writes no indent in front of a row, so jiro keeps the rows raw.
-- input.jira --
||h||
|a\\
 |b|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>a<br class="atl-forced-newline" /></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>b</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
:::table
||h||
|a\\
 |b|
:::
-- warnings.json --
[]
